cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Predicting 30-Day Hospital Readmission in Medicare Patients: An Interpretable XGBoost Model on MIMIC-IV v3.1"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bandeira"
    given-names: "Thiago"
    affiliation: "Florida International University, Miami, FL, USA"
    email: "tbati006@fiu.edu"
  - family-names: "Gonzalez"
    given-names: "Armando"
    affiliation: "Florida International University, Miami, FL, USA"
  - family-names: "Poellabauer"
    given-names: "Christian"
    affiliation: "Florida International University, Miami, FL, USA"
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  A reproducible XGBoost pipeline for predicting 30-day all-cause readmission
  in Medicare patients using MIMIC-IV v3.1. Parsimonious 50-feature model
  trained under a strict 60/20/20 patient-grouped train/validation/test
  protocol, with SHAP-based interpretability and benchmarking against LACE
  and ClinicalBERT.
keywords:
  - "30-day readmission"
  - "Medicare"
  - "MIMIC-IV"
  - "gradient boosting"
  - "XGBoost"
  - "SHAP"
  - "interpretable machine learning"
  - "clinical decision support"
